  "description": "Arkcon welcomes you to our  studio apartment to let on the ever popular St Lawrence Road. Please email your enquiry. Phone call enquires are not accepted due to high volume demand. We aim to respond to all enquiries, however this may not be possible. Thank you for your understanding. \n\nBoasting original yet modern features, these are the highest quality of studios on the rental market today. Upon entering the studios your immediately met with high ceilings, open plan space and bespoke high end kitchens. The bathrooms as seen in the photos are spacious and promote modern and detailed interior finish. This house is beyond compare and full of surprises from the minute you walk in the front door. Free on street parking, WiFi and bins collection is available. \n\nSt Lawrence Road needs little introduction as being one of Clontarf's premier roads. With the Howth Road at the top and the Clontarf Road at the bottom, the location is outstanding and the convenience hard to beat. Number 36 is also on the West facing side of the road so on top of being a striking red brick period property it also has a sunny rear garden. Clontarf is a coastal suburb on the northside of Dublin. It has a range of commercial facilities mainly centred on Vernon Avenue. Clontarf's most notable amenity is its seafront, with a promenade running continuously from Alfie Byrne Road to the wooden bridge at Dollymount. As well as extensive walks and green areas, St Anne's Park is nearby and is the second largest municipal park in Dublin. \n\nPlease email your enquiry to make this property your own. References and documents are required by all applicants. Bills are not included in the monthly rent. Bins collection is inclusive. Thank you.",
